# Shell scripts must reach a Mac with LF endings.
#
# Measured twice. On 2026-08-03 a build script went to pub.dev with CRLF and
# exited zero having built nothing. On 2026-08-04 the same script, checked out
# on Windows, killed a macOS build on its first line:
#
#   apple/build_rust.sh: line 32: $'\r': command not found
#   apple/build_rust.sh: line 33: set: -$'\r'
#
# Both times the git *index* held LF and only the checkout was wrong, which is
# why a diff shows nothing and a review cannot see it. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# — the default on Windows — and no rule here, every checkout re-arms it.
#
# It reaches consumers because `flutter pub publish` packs the **working tree**,
# not the index: whatever is on the publishing machine's disk is what every
# Apple consumer downloads. `pub publish --dry-run` does not check line endings,
# so the gate stays green while the package is unbuildable.
#
# Dart, Rust, C and CMake all tolerate CRLF. A shell script does not, so it is
# the only thing pinned here.
*.sh text eol=lf
